@startuml sequence-US8

autonumber

actor "Student" as Student
participant "Flask route\n(/listings)" as Route
participant "Listing model" as Listing
database "PostgreSQL\n(listings)" as DB

Student -> Route: GET /listings?tags=vegan,halal&location=Student Union
activate Route
Route -> Route: read the selected dietary tags and campus location from the query string
Route -> Listing: available listings matching every filter
activate Listing
Listing -> DB: SELECT * FROM listings\nWHERE cancelled = false AND pickup_end not ended\nAND portions_total - portions_reserved > 0
activate DB
DB --> Listing: still available rows
deactivate DB
Listing --> Route: filtered in the view: only listings that have ALL selected tags\nand, when chosen, are at the selected campus location,\nsorted by pickup window end
deactivate Listing

alt No listing matches the filters
    Route --> Student: empty state "No food listings are currently available."
else At least one listing matches
    Route --> Student: the matching listings
end
deactivate Route

Student -> Route: GET /listings (Clear filters)
activate Route
Route -> Route: drop the tag and location filters
Route -> Listing: available listings with no filter
activate Listing
Listing -> DB: SELECT * FROM listings\nWHERE cancelled = false AND pickup_end not ended\nAND portions_total - portions_reserved > 0\nORDER BY pickup_end ASC
activate DB
DB --> Listing: every available listing
deactivate DB
Listing --> Route: unfiltered listings
deactivate Listing
Route --> Student: all available listings are shown again
deactivate Route

@enduml
